	url = {https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1468-0394.1995.tb00271.x},
	doi = {10.1111/j.1468-0394.1995.tb00271.x},
	abstract = {Abstract:
              There is still a need for new knowledge elicitation techniques and tools. Laddering is a technique which has a long history in a wide range of disciplines and which has proved extremely useful in knowledge elicitation. There have, however, been few attempts to describe and survey the technique per se.
            
            
              This paper describes the technique, its background, its use, analysis, and automation, with particular reference to knowledge elicitation. The advantages and disadvantages of the technique are described. It is concluded that laddering is a valuable technique which could be used in a wide range of settings.},
